Qus.5 -> Why do we use meta tags?
Sol -> 
   Meta tags are used in HTML to provide metadata (information about the webpage) to browsers and search engines. They are placed inside the <head> section of an HTML document.
Key Reasons for Using Meta Tags:

    SEO (Search Engine Optimization) – Helps search engines understand the page content (e.g., <meta name="description">).
    Character Encoding – Ensures proper text display (e.g., <meta charset="UTF-8">).
    Responsive Design – Makes the page mobile-friendly (e.g., <meta name="viewport">).
    Social Media Integration – Defines how the page appears on platforms like Facebook and Twitter (e.g., Open Graph tags).
    Automatic Refresh & Redirection – Can refresh or redirect a page after a set time (e.g., <meta http-equiv="refresh">).

Example of Meta Tags in HTML:

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="description" content="This is a sample webpage with meta tags.">
    <meta name="keywords" content="HTML, meta tags, SEO, web development">
    <meta name="author" content="John Doe">
</head>